statement:
Let \(n,d\in\mathbb Z_{>0}\), and retain the exact canonical hard pooled KKT system, notation, normalizations, and alias maps of accepted facts 236e5d1f3c2efa28, 637b5f7874d8c875, 0ba2ef9056bea8b9, 6a74481cad1d7e81, and e8b320da9989469f. Thus the finite canonical edge set has midpoint target bodies \(L_e\subseteq\mathbb R^d\), centered gauge bodies \(D_e\subseteq\mathbb R^d\), reservoir weights \(r_e\geq0\), original load-minimal vectors \(v_e\), and original loads
\[
 \omega_e:=h_{D_e}(v_e),
 \qquad 0\leq\omega_e\leq r_e,
 \qquad Q:=\sum_e r_e>0,
 \qquad \Omega:=\sum_e\omega_e.
\tag{1}
\]
Retain the target multipliers and congestion charge
\[
 0<\chi_m\leq1,
 \qquad \lambda_e:=1-\chi_{m_e},
 \qquad \beta_e:=\beta_e^{\mathrm{cong}}
 :=\lambda_e\omega_e,
 \qquad B:=B_{\mathrm{cong}}:=\sum_e\beta_e.
\tag{2}
\]
For a nonnegative edge field \(q\), write
\[
 R_C(q):=
 \max_{s:\mathbb R^n\to\mathbb R^d\ {\rm affine}}
 \sum_{e:\,s(m_e)\in L_e}q_e.
\tag{3}
\]
In the present positive-fresh branch, the fresh load-minimal reoptimization of accepted fact 6a74481cad1d7e81 has
\[
 \widetilde\Omega:=\widetilde\Omega_{\mathrm{cong}}>0.
\tag{4}
\]
Consequently \(B>0\). Put
\[
 C_\beta:=R_C(\beta),
 \qquad
 \mathcal U_\beta:=
 \max_s\sum_{\substack{e:\,\beta_e>0\\s(m_e)\in L_e}}r_e.
\tag{5}
\]
Let
\[
 A:=\max\{P_{\mathrm{pool}},P_{\mathrm{anc}}\},
 \qquad
 F_{\mathrm{fr}}
 :=2^{n-\widetilde\rho_{\mathrm{cong}}}
 \frac{\widetilde\Omega}
 {\widetilde r_{\mathrm{cong}}+1}
\tag{6}
\]
be the exact ancestral and fresh quantities of accepted fact 637b5f7874d8c875. Retain the positive-fresh ancestral rank \(r_{\mathrm{anc}}\), ancestral base rank \(\rho_{\mathrm{anc}}\), and drift rank \(k_{\mathrm{drift}}\) of accepted fact e8b320da9989469f.

Retain the same-ray negative-circuit decomposition of accepted fact 236e5d1f3c2efa28. Namely, for every original positive-load edge \(e\), set
\[
 u_e:=\frac{v_e}{\omega_e},
 \qquad h_{D_e}(u_e)=1,
\tag{7}
\]
and there are nonnegative coefficients \(\omega_e^{(j)}\), vectors
\[
 v_e^{(j)}:=\omega_e^{(j)}u_e,
 \qquad
 C_j:=\{e:\omega_e^{(j)}>0\},
 \qquad 1\leq j\leq N,
\tag{8}
\]
such that every \(C_j\) is nonempty,
\[
 \sum_j\omega_e^{(j)}=\omega_e,
 \qquad
 \sum_ev_e^{(j)}=0,
 \qquad
 \sum_ev_e^{(j)}m_e^{\mathsf T}=0,
 \qquad
 \sum_{e\in C_j}h_{L_e}(v_e^{(j)})<0.
\tag{9}
\]
Define
\[
 \delta_j:=\min_{e\in C_j}\lambda_e\omega_e^{(j)},
 \qquad
 \mathcal B_{\mathrm{circ}}:=\sum_{j=1}^N\delta_j,
 \qquad
 \tau_j:=\min_{e\in C_j}\lambda_e.
\tag{10}
\]

First, define the uniformly circuit-scaled ancestral field
\[
 w_e^{\circ}:=\sum_{j=1}^N\tau_jv_e^{(j)},
 \qquad
 \theta_e:=h_{D_e}(w_e^{\circ}).
\tag{11}
\]
Then all sums in (11) are same-ray sums and
\[
 \boxed{
 \theta_e=\sum_j\tau_j\omega_e^{(j)}
 \leq\lambda_e\omega_e=\beta_e,}
\tag{12}
\]
\[
 \boxed{
 \sum_ew_e^{\circ}=0,
 \qquad
 \sum_ew_e^{\circ}m_e^{\mathsf T}=0.}
\tag{13}
\]
Thus \(w^{\circ}\) is feasible for the fresh weighted dual on \(\beta\), using no edge beyond its one congestion capacity. Its total gauge load satisfies
\[
 \boxed{
 \Theta_{\circ}:=\sum_e\theta_e
 =\sum_j\tau_j\sum_{e\in C_j}\omega_e^{(j)}
 \geq\sum_j\delta_j
 =\mathcal B_{\mathrm{circ}}.}
\tag{14}
\]
Moreover,
\[
 \boxed{
 \sum_eh_{L_e}(w_e^{\circ})
 =\sum_j\tau_j
 \sum_{e\in C_j}h_{L_e}(v_e^{(j)}).}
\tag{15}
\]
If \(\mathcal B_{\mathrm{circ}}>0\), the common value in (15) is strictly negative. In particular, uniform whole-circuit scaling supplies a legal positive dual witness without deleting any edge of a contributing circuit.

Second, put
\[
 J_+:=\{j:\delta_j>0\}.
\tag{16}
\]
For every \(j\in J_+\), there is an inclusion-minimal set
\[
 I_j\subseteq C_j,
 \qquad k_j:=|I_j|\geq2,
\tag{17}
\]
such that no affine map \(s:\mathbb R^n\to\mathbb R^d\) satisfies
\[
 s(m_e)\in L_e\qquad(e\in I_j).
\tag{18}
\]
Every edge of \(I_j\) has \(\beta_e>0\). For every \(e\in I_j\), there is an affine map \(s_{j,e}\) satisfying
\[
 s_{j,e}(m_f)\in L_f
 \qquad(f\in I_j\setminus\{e\}).
\tag{19}
\]
Writing
\[
 \beta(I):=\sum_{e\in I}\beta_e,
 \qquad
 r(I):=\sum_{e\in I}r_e,
\tag{20}
\]
these genuine affine non-hit families satisfy the exact local bounds
\[
 \boxed{
 \beta(I_j)\leq\frac{k_j}{k_j-1}C_\beta,
 \qquad
 r(I_j)\leq\frac{k_j}{k_j-1}\mathcal U_\beta,}
\tag{21}
\]
and hence
\[
 \boxed{
 (k_j-1)\delta_j\leq C_\beta\leq\mathcal U_\beta.}
\tag{22}
\]
The bottlenecks form an exact fractional packing under the original congestion capacities:
\[
 \boxed{
 \sum_{\substack{j\in J_+\\e\in I_j}}\delta_j
 \leq\beta_e
 \qquad(e).}
\tag{23}
\]
Consequently,
\[
 \boxed{
 \sum_{j\in J_+}k_j\delta_j\leq B,
 \qquad
 \sum_{j\in J_+}(k_j-1)\delta_j
 \leq B-\mathcal B_{\mathrm{circ}}.}
\tag{24}
\]
More particularly, for every arbitrary choice of one omitted edge \(a_j\in I_j\) for each \(j\in J_+\),
\[
 \boxed{
 \sum_{j:\,a_j=e}\delta_j\leq\beta_e
 \quad(e),
 \qquad
 \sum_{j\in J_+}\delta_j=\mathcal B_{\mathrm{circ}}.}
\tag{25}
\]
Thus even a circuitwise choice of indispensable edges does not reuse an edge capacity.

Third, the support-lifted exact three-capacity ledger is
\[
 \boxed{
 D+R+R_{\mathrm{sel}}(C)
 \geq
 A+\max\{Q-\Omega,\mathcal U_\beta\}
 +\max\{A,F_{\mathrm{fr}}\}.}
\tag{26}
\]
In the canonical hard branch this gives the strict screen
\[
 \boxed{
 A+\max\{Q-\Omega,\mathcal U_\beta\}
 +\max\{A,F_{\mathrm{fr}}\}<\frac Q{100},}
\tag{27}
\]
so in particular
\[
 A<\frac Q{200},
 \qquad
 C_\beta\leq\mathcal U_\beta<\frac Q{100},
 \qquad
 F_{\mathrm{fr}}<\frac Q{100}.
\tag{28}
\]
The accepted positive-fresh circuit/drift chain remains
\[
 \boxed{
 F_{\mathrm{fr}}
 \geq
 2^{n-\widetilde\rho_{\mathrm{cong}}}
 \frac{B-C_\beta}{r_{\mathrm{anc}}+k_{\mathrm{drift}}+1}
 \geq
 2^{n-\widetilde\rho_{\mathrm{cong}}}
 \frac{\mathcal B_{\mathrm{circ}}}
 {r_{\mathrm{anc}}+k_{\mathrm{drift}}+1}
 \geq
 2^{n-\rho_{\mathrm{anc}}}
 \frac{\mathcal B_{\mathrm{circ}}}
 {r_{\mathrm{anc}}+k_{\mathrm{drift}}+1}.}
\tag{29}
\]

Equations (12)-(15) are a legal same-ray compensation, and (21)-(25) are a legal no-reuse allocation. They do not prove \(\mathfrak S_{\mathrm{split}}\geq\Omega/99\). The maps \(s_{j,e}\) in (19) may depend on both \(j\) and \(e\), whereas \(\mathcal U_\beta\) is one maximum charged to the single capacity \(R\) in (26). Therefore neither \(\sum_j\mathcal U_\beta\) nor a sum of the separate local hit masses in (19) is authorized. Likewise \(A\) and \(F_{\mathrm{fr}}\) are competing lower bounds inside the one maximum assigned to \(R_{\mathrm{sel}}(C)\); they cannot be added. The missing implication is precisely a common-affine realization or a terminal absorption of the fractionally packed families \(I_j\). Thus the broad split-retention-circuit-closure subgoal remains open.
